# WorkLog user lifecycle and frontend implementation guide

This guide is written from the WorkLog API, Supabase migrations, and service
code in this repository. It documents the current backend contract and the
frontend screens needed to use it.

The repository contains the WorkLog API and SQL migrations, not the WorkLog
frontend implementation. Screen and route names below are requirements and
examples; they are not claims that those frontend pages already exist.
WorkLog's database model is defined by the Supabase migrations. There are no
WorkLog Mongoose models in this repository.

## Code and schema sources

Use these as the canonical sources when this guide and implementation differ:

- `../routes/worklog/worklog.routes.js`: health, profile bootstrap,
  organization creation and details.
- `../routes/worklog/data.routes.js` and `../services/worklog/dataService.js`:
  business data routes, field validation, API-to-database field mapping,
  optimistic concurrency, and archive behavior.
- `../routes/worklog/management.routes.js`: memberships, invitations, roles,
  permissions, and settings.
- `../services/worklog/organizationService.js`: profile synchronization,
  membership lookup, organization creation.
- `../services/worklog/invitationService.js`: invitation token, email, and
  redirect URL behavior.
- `../middleware/worklogAuth.js`: bearer authentication and permission check.
- `../supabase/migrations/001_initial_worklog_schema.sql` through
  `../supabase/migrations/004_worklog_invitations.sql`: actual tables,
